<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Euphemius</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 828</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Euphemius was a Byzantine naval commander in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a> who rebelled against the emperor Michael II in 826 and proclaimed himself emperor. Defeated by loyal forces, he invited the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aghlabid-dynasty">Aghlabids</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ifriqiya">Ifriqiya</a> to intervene, and their invasion in 827 began the Muslim conquest of Sicily. He was killed by Byzantine defenders around 828.</p></div>
